KW  - Dynamic graph generation
KW  - Graph convolutional network
AB  - Spatio-temporal forecasting can provide valuable insights for traffic optimization, energy management, and environmental governance. However, capturing complex and intertwined spatio-temporal dependencies is challenging due to two main factors: the entanglement of trend and fluctuation within the spatio-temporal series and the dynamic changes in inter-series relationships. To address these issues, an Adaptive Trend–Fluctuation Decomposition based Dual-Branch Graph Network (ATFD2BGN) is proposed to capture the spatio-temporal features of trend and fluctuation components, utilizing singular spectrum analysis and dual-branch graph network. To achieve effective decomposition, ATFD2BGN employs singular spectrum analysis, which adaptively identifies and distinguishes the features of trend and fluctuation, enabling precise decomposition. Then, based on the global stability of the trend component and the local dynamic characteristics of the fluctuation component, we designed appropriate feature extraction strategies to capture the spatio-temporal patterns of each component. Furthermore, we model the dynamic spatial correlations between series by constructing dynamic graph structures. Finally, we apply gated fusion to combine the trend and fluctuation components for spatio-temporal forecasting. Extensive experiments on several real-world spatio-temporal datasets are conducted and the results show that ATFD2BGN achieves state-of-the-art performance with up to 3.22% improvement on PEMS07 in addition to providing interpretability for analyzing the series components.
ER  - 

